{
 "_readme": [
  "How a garment from the feed is matched to one of Catherine's 100 checklist rows.",
  "",
  "ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH, and it is applied ONCE. scripts/slot_match.py reads these",
  "rules at INGEST time and stores the answer in products.slots, so the live shelf",
  "does a single indexed lookup ('slots contains to1') and cannot possibly disagree",
  "with the report that measured it. ⚠️ The tempting alternative -- have the shelf",
  "re-derive the match in JavaScript on every tap -- would put one rule in two",
  "programs, and a rule that lives in two places drifts. This project has paid for",
  "that lesson more than once (the store table vs SEARCH_DOMAINS, the eight",
  "footers, the five copies of the colour-preference bullet).",
  "▶ THE COST, honestly: a change here does not reach the shop until the next",
  "  nightly run, or a hand-dispatched one. At most a day, against a whole class of",
  "  bug that then cannot happen.",
  "",
  "THE LADDER, and it exists because MEASUREMENT SAID NO SINGLE COLUMN IS FILLED IN",
  "AT EVERY STORE (see docs/product-feeds-plan.md). A garment matches when either:",
  "  cat  -- a term appears in its category path (merchant_category, then",
  "          category_secondary, then category_primary, joined and lowercased), or",
  "  name -- a term appears in its product NAME.",
  "The name rung is not a nicety: Marissa Collections is 8,755 garments, 11% of the",
  "whole catalog, with NO category, NO colour, NO material and NO pattern. The name",
  "is genuinely all there is, so any row that cannot be matched by name is a row",
  "that silently loses a ninth of the shop.",
  "",
  "🚨 A `cat` TERM MUST BE AS SPECIFIC AS THE ROW. The ladder is cat OR name, so a",
  "DEPARTMENT-WIDE term on a row that is only a SUBSET of that department matches",
  "the whole department. Measured on 2026-09-05: 'sleepwear' on Robes made every",
  "pyjama set a robe, 'activewear' on ten rows made one pair of leggings also a",
  "sports bra and an athletic sock, 'earrings' on three rows made one pair of hoops",
  "also a stud, and 'underwear' on Shapewear pulled in ski socks and tights.",
  "▶ Use the merchant's specific leaf ('sandals>flat sandals'), not the department.",
  "  The one exception is a row with a COLOUR or PATTERN gate, which really is the",
  "  whole department narrowed by that gate -- and scripts/test_slot_match.py",
  "  enforces exactly that distinction so the trap cannot come back.",
  "",
  "not     -- rejects, checked against the category path AND the name. This is where",
  "           her category-boundary rules live (White tops must not be a tank, a",
  "           blouse or a going-out top -- her own 2026-08-15 finding).",
  "color   -- if present, the colour field or the name must carry one of these. Kept",
  "           LOOSE on purpose: colour is recorded 663 ways, is 15% blank, disagrees",
  "           on capitals, and at FARM Rio it is a PRINT NAME ('TROPICAL GROOVE",
  "           BLUE') rather than a colour.",
  "pattern -- if present, the pattern column must be one of these. ⚠️ pattern is",
  "           blank at five of the seven stores, so it may RANK but must never GATE",
  "           anywhere except the rows that are actually about pattern.",
  "",
  "Matching is word-boundary and de-pluralized on BOTH sides, so 'Dresses' meets",
  "'dress' and ' top ' is never found inside 'laptop'. See scripts/slot_match.py.",
  "",
  "⚠️ THE ROWS THEMSELVES ARE HERS AND SO ARE THE BOUNDARIES. Do not invent a new",
  "exclusion because a shelf looks untidy -- bring her the row and ask, the same",
  "standing rule as the store tags. The Tops and Work-appropriate-dresses rules",
  "below are transcribed from _WDR_IDEA_EXCLUDE in index.html, which is her work.",
  "",
  "▶ AFTER ANY CHANGE HERE: run the 'Rakuten checklist coverage' workflow, which",
  "  prints every row's garment count and three real sample names. An empty row is",
  "  a broken rule; a wrong row is only visible in the samples."
 ],
